<section class="page-hero page-hero-compact">
  <div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Terms</p>
    <h1>The short<br><em>print.</em></h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      Ei Void is a developer preview with two pillars: reminders and an
      on-device coding agent. Use it carefully, keep your own backups, and do not
      treat a preview as a warranty.
    </p>
    <p class="page-meta">Last updated 21 November 2026 · developer preview</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell prose">
    <h2>The preview</h2>
    <p>
      Ei Void is provided as a developer preview under the MIT licence. Features,
      plans, data formats and hosted services may change or disappear. Nothing
      here is a promise of uptime, fitness for a particular purpose or a
      particular model.
    </p>

    <h2>Reminders</h2>
    <p>
      Reminders are a convenience, not a financial service. A missed
      notification does not make Ei Void responsible for a late payment, fee or
      credit consequence. Check the due date yourself when the amount matters.
      Do not use the reminder feature for emergency or safety-critical
      notifications.
    </p>

    <h2>Your keys, your providers</h2>
    <p>
      You bring your own AI provider keys and your own GitHub account. You are
      responsible for the costs, terms and data handling of those providers and
      for the repositories you point the agent at. Do not use Ei Void on code you
      are not allowed to send to the provider you configured.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not use the bot or website to spam, harass, scrape other users, evade
      rate limits, or attack the host or Discord. Do not put a bot token,
      provider key or GitHub token in a public issue, a commit or a client-side
      bundle. Do not use the bot to process other people's private data without
      their consent.
    </p>

    <h2>The agent can be wrong</h2>
    <p>
      Model output can be incorrect, insecure or destructive. Review the diff.
      The app asks before delete and push, but the confirmation is your
      responsibility. Keep the code in git; keep a backup that is not only the
      phone.
    </p>

    <h2>Plans and payment</h2>
    <p>
      The plans shown are a preview. No checkout is live, no card is collected,
      and no subscription is created. Future paid plans will have their own
      terms, taxes and cancellation rules before billing starts.
    </p>

    <h2>The website and bot</h2>
    <p>
      The website is a companion, not a backup service. It stores the Clerk
      identity, reminder snapshot, Discord identity and usage counters, and does
      not store repository content or keys. Link codes are single-use and expire.
      Do not share a link URL; it is a temporary door to your dashboard.
    </p>

    <h2>Open source</h2>
    <p>
      The source is under the MIT licence in the repository. The cat artwork is
      part of this project's identity; do not imply endorsement by Ei Void when
      you fork it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may change with the preview. Open an issue in the
      <a class="text-link" href="<%= site.repoUrl %>" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Ei Void repository</a>
      for questions.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
